WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.275 --> 00:00:16.456
old man told everyone about Dr.

2
00:00:16.476 --> 00:00:20.458
Dolittle. Everyone wanted to bring their animals to him.

3
00:00:21.399 --> 00:00:22.299
Soon Dr.

4
00:00:22.359 --> 00:00:25.201
Dolittle became known as the animal doctor.

5
00:00:26.321 --> 00:00:30.784
His sister, Sarah, was happy again because now they had plenty of money.

6
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.781
Farmers came from miles away to see him.

7
00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:39.702
"I don't know what's wrong with him, Doctor," one murmured.

8
00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:43.643
"I've been trying to tell him for weeks now!"

9
00:00:44.203 --> 00:00:45.323
the horse complained.

10
00:00:45.343 --> 00:00:47.664
"You must be patient.

11
00:00:47.944 --> 00:00:49.324
He doesn't understand," Dr.

12
00:00:49.904 --> 00:00:52.225
Dolittle gently reminded the animal.

13
00:00:58.167 --> 00:00:59.707
the problem with humans!"

14
00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:00.907
said the horse.

15
00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.848
"They just don't listen!"

16
00:01:03.984 --> 00:01:08.045
"Now, now, let's take a look at you," the doctor kindly replied.

17
00:01:08.065 --> 00:01:12.186
"Look! He's giving me pills for diarrhea!"

18
00:01:16.647 --> 00:01:19.408
The doctor soon realized the horse's problem.

19
00:01:20.188 --> 00:01:22.609
"You have poor eyesight," Dr.

20
00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.489
Dolittle said.

21
00:01:23.509 --> 00:01:28.491
"YES! I need glasses, not diarrhea pills!"

22
00:01:29.011 --> 00:01:30.291
he sighed with relief.

23
00:01:30.311 --> 00:01:35.681
"I'll get you a pair then," and he wrote in his notebook.

24
00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:37.862
"I like yours.

25
00:01:38.302 --> 00:01:39.742
Can I get some like that?"

26
00:01:40.223 --> 00:01:41.623
the horse nudged Dr.

27
00:01:41.663 --> 00:01:42.744
Dolittle's glasses.

28
00:01:42.764 --> 00:01:44.784
"Yes, they are rather nice.

29
00:01:45.165 --> 00:01:47.205
I'll see what I can do," said Dr.

30
00:01:47.245 --> 00:01:52.668
Dolittle. A week later, the horse returned with the farmer.

31
00:01:52.688 --> 00:01:56.709
"I got green glasses for you," Dr.

32
00:01:56.729 --> 00:01:58.690
Dolittle said as he put them on.

33
00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:02.371
"I just love the color green!

34
00:02:02.972 --> 00:02:03.472
Thank you!"

35
00:02:03.808 --> 00:02:04.629
he smiled.

36
00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:08.231
"There! How's that?

37
00:02:08.611 --> 00:02:09.612
Can you see better?"

38
00:02:10.172 --> 00:02:10.972
asked the doctor.

39
00:02:10.992 --> 00:02:13.154
"Crystal clear!

40
00:02:13.614 --> 00:02:15.995
You really are amazing, Dr.

41
00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.896
Dolittle,"said the horse.

42
00:02:18.677 --> 00:02:23.460
Soon it was not unusual to see horses wearing glasses around Puddleby.

43
00:02:26.782 --> 00:02:29.723
All the animals told their family and friends about Dr.

44
00:02:31.272 --> 00:02:33.893
Dolittle. His garden was always crowded with animals.

45
00:02:34.914 --> 00:02:36.955
There were so many that Dr.

46
00:02:37.015 --> 00:02:39.357
Dolittle put up signs for each animal.

47
00:02:39.377 --> 00:02:43.519
"All cows stand here!

48
00:02:43.539 --> 00:02:45.280
Horses, there!

49
00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.541
Sheep, over there, please!"

50
00:02:48.341 --> 00:02:49.622
Polynesia called out.

51
00:02:50.683 --> 00:02:53.104
Dr. Dolittle's other pets helped him, too.

52
00:02:53.124 --> 00:02:55.906
"Hey! It's not your turn!

53
00:02:56.266 --> 00:02:59.848
Get back in line," Jip growled to a straying cow.

54
00:03:01.136 --> 00:03:06.060
"Okay, next horse, please come this way," Gub-Gub called out.

55
00:03:07.961 --> 00:03:11.023
Dr. Dolittle saw the bigger animals in his garden.

56
00:03:11.744 --> 00:03:14.265
His office was for the smallest of creatures.

57
00:03:14.966 --> 00:03:20.570
Mice, raccoons, badgers, and squirrels all waited in line to see the doctor.

58
00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:25.773
"You've got to stop eating food from the garbage," Dr.

59
00:03:25.813 --> 00:03:27.474
Dolittle told a little mouse.

60
00:03:27.494 --> 00:03:29.376
"But I'm hungry!"

61
00:03:30.012 --> 00:03:30.912
the mouse cried.

62
00:03:31.873 --> 00:03:35.254
Try to find something fresh like fruits or vegetables then."

63
00:03:36.035 --> 00:03:38.916
The mouse felt better after taking some medicine.

64
00:03:40.797 --> 00:03:42.137
Every night Dr.

65
00:03:42.197 --> 00:03:45.498
Dolittle was very tired but he was very happy.

66
00:03:45.518 --> 00:03:49.520
"You're famous all over Puddleby," said Gub-Gub.

67
00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:53.982
"Famous all over the world," Too-Too hooted.

68
00:03:54.002 --> 00:04:00.357
"Some friends of mine from England have heard of you," explained the owl.

69
00:04:00.377 --> 00:04:05.102
"If only more humans could speak our language," sighed Jip.

70
00:04:05.782 --> 00:04:08.525
"Still, there would never be anyone like Dr.

71
00:04:08.585 --> 00:04:11.068
Dolittle," Polynesia remarked.

72
00:04:11.088 --> 00:04:19.496
"ZZZZZZ the doctor mumbled.
